melody:
# Chorus (the original is in cut time; written here with quarter-note beats)
Here's the Jap-a-nese
C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5
Sand-man, sneak-ing on with the dew,
A4(2) A4(2) ~A4 C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 A4(4) ~A4
just an old sec-ond hand man,
C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 D5(2) C5(2) ~C5/
he'll buy your old day from you.
A4/ C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ G4 F4(4)
He will take ev-'ry sor-row
r C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 A4(2) A4(2) ~A4
of the day that is through,
C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 C#5(4) ~C#5
and he'll give you to-mor-row
E5/ C#5/ E5/ C#5/ E5 C#5(2) B4(2) ~B4
just to start life a-new.
B4/ G#4/ B4/ G#4/ B4 A4(4) ~A4/
Then you'll be a bit old-er
r/ C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 A4(2) A4(2) ~A4
in the dawn when you wake,
C5/ D5/ C5/ A4/ G4 F4(4) ~F4
and you'll be a bit bold-er
A4/ F4/ A4/ F4/ A4 F4(2) F4(2) ~F4
with the new day you make.
A4/ F4/ A4/ F4/ A4 E4(4) ~E4
Here's the Jap-a-nese Sand-man,
C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 A4(2) A4(2) ~A4
trade him sil-ver for gold,
C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ C5 F5(4) ~F5/
just an old sec-ond hand man,
r/ D5/ A4/ D5/ A4/ D5 A4(2) A4(2) ~A4/
trad-ing new days for old.
r/ C5/ A4/ C5/ A4/ G4 F4(4)

